-- title:
--   From HTo GAdjacent Stage M3 E Paper Move
-- statement:
--   **The M3-to-E adjacent-stage move is controlled by the self-consistency error.**
--
--   Let `params` have a field model, let `psi_bi` be a normalized bipartite state, and let `family` be an indexed polynomial submeasurement family. Let $\gamma,\zeta$ be error parameters. Assume `GHatFactsStatement params psi_bi family gamma zeta` and the exact adjacent-stage facts for `family`. Then, for any natural numbers $k,\ell$,
--
--   $$
--   \left|\operatorname{fromHToGAdjacentStageM3}(\mathrm{params},\psi_{\mathrm{bi}},\mathrm{family},k,\ell)-\operatorname{fromHToGStageMass}(\mathrm{params},\psi_{\mathrm{bi}},\mathrm{family},k,\ell+1)\right|
--   \le \sqrt{2\zeta}.
--   $$
--
--   This is the final analytic and collapse estimate that replaces the M3 expression by the next recurrence stage in `fromHToGAdjacentStage_paperMoveChain`.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.fromHToGAdjacentStageM3E_paperMove`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
